WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:05.790
NCIS: New Orleans' newest Special Agent, Tammy
Gregorio, has quickly became a favorite with

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:10.019
fans, some of whom were surely left wondering
where they'd seen actress Vanessa Ferlito

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:10.660
before.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.760
"Put your hands up!

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:13.760
Now!"

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:18.920
NCIS: New Orleans definitely isn't Ferlito's
debut — here's where we've seen this Brooklynite

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:20.130
before.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.340
24

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:27.490
Ferlito scored an early breakout role on the
hit Fox crime drama 24, appearing on 11 episodes

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:32.550
of the show's third season as Claudia Hernandez,
Hector Salazar's girlfriend and secret lover

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:36.250
of the show's protagonist, Jack Bauer, played
by Kiefer Sutherland.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:40.370
Claudia agreed to help Bauer in exchange for
passage out of Mexico, but she was killed

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:41.370
in the process.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:45.800
According to Ferlito, Claudia wasn't originally
supposed to die, and she and Jack would have

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:46.800
ended up together.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:51.480
But her character was killed off after Ferlito
was cast in the 2005 Tommy Lee Jones crime

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.390
comedy called...

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:54.920
Man of the House

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:59.340
Given the movie's abysmal nine percent Rotten
Tomatoes score, Ferlito may have ended up

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.120
wishing she'd stayed on 24.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.050
Then again, Ferlito may have taken some small
comfort from the fact that her performance

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:08.810
in Man of the House was one of the few things
in the critical and commercial dud to earn

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:09.940
positive notice.

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:14.380
While strenuously urging potential viewers
to stay away, Variety noted that she stood

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.660
out among the ensemble supporting Jones,

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:20.520
"…mainly because she's the only one who
gets enough to do to make a strong impression

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:23.030
as a distinctive personality."

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:24.780
Spider-Man 2

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:28.780
Like most hard-working actors, Ferlito has
occasionally appeared in projects that only

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:29.930
featured her briefly.

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:33.570
Take, for example, her part in 2004's Spider-Man
2.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:38.360
In the superhero sequel, Ferlito played Louise,
Mary Jane's friend and shopping partner.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:42.440
It's a small part, but at least Ferlito fans
can enjoy this extended scene featuring her

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:45.860
chatting with Mary Jane that was edited out
of the theatrical cut.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:48.170
"What about that perfect kiss you had once?

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:49.220
The guy you believed in?"

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:51.060
"That was a fantasy."

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:52.420
Shadowboxer

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:57.420
In 2005, Ferlito landed a role as Stephen
Dorff's pregnant wife in the crime thriller

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:01.700
Shadowboxer — and like her other big-screen
feature that year, Man of the House, it was

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:03.030
critically panned.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:04.730
Slant dismissed it as, quote,

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:08.450
"...a faux-art-house crime thriller, and the
closest approximation the movies have offered

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:11.910
audiences this year of feeling trapped inside
a rancid toilet bowl."

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:15.620
That's some pretty scathing criticism, but
Ferlito was hardly the focus.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:20.650
Shadowboxer had some far bigger names attached,
including Academy Award winners Cuba Gooding

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:22.250
Jr. and Helen Mirren.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:23.400
CSI: New York

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:28.640
NCIS: New Orleans isn't the first primetime
crime drama to prominently feature Vanessa

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:29.670
Ferlito.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:31.950
That honor goes to CSI: New York.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:36.660
Ferlito appeared on 26 episodes of the long-running
spinoff series before her character, Aiden

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:37.890
Burn, was murdered.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:41.290
She later claimed that it was her decision
to leave, telling TV Guide,

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:43.900
"I had no intention of doing an hour TV show.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:47.680
I had just wrapped the movie Man of the House
with Tommy Lee Jones, so it's not like I had

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:48.680
nothing going on.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:50.170
But it was CSI: New York!

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.990
You don't say no to that."

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:53.680
Death Proof

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:57.430
Ferlito's first few big-screen roles may not
have turned out the way she'd hoped, but all

00:02:57.430 --> 00:03:02.720
that early experience paid off in 2007 with
a part in Quentin Tarantino's Death Proof.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:07.180
Ferlito played Arlene, aka "Butterfly," one
of three friends killed by Stuntman Kurt Russell

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.080
and his "death-proof" stunt car.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:13.460
In an interview with ACED magazine, she claimed
Tarantino wrote the role of Butterfly specifically

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:14.460
for her.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.320
Ferlito is responsible for one of Death Proof's
most talked about scenes, in which Butterfly

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:20.230
gives Stuntman Mike a lap dance.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:21.230
She told ACED,

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:23.380
"People still go crazy over that lap dance.

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:24.540
It has a cult following now."

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:27.319
Madea Goes to Jail

00:03:27.319 --> 00:03:31.600
After working with Quentin Tarantino, Ferlito
stepped in front of the cameras for a different

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:36.370
sort of auteur, playing a heroin-addicted
prostitute named Donna in Tyler Perry's Madea

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:37.370
Goes to Jail.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:41.251
Ferlito later told Trailer Addict she loved
working with Perry, specifically because she

00:03:41.251 --> 00:03:44.390
appreciates working with directors who are
also actors.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:48.560
Like most of Perry's directorial efforts,
Madea Goes to Jail proved profitable at the

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:53.370
box office, so it's safe to assume that more
than a few NCIS: New Orleans viewers recognize

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.910
Ferlito from this big-screen hit.

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:58.030
Wall Street: Money Never Sleeps

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:02.250
Sharing a few minutes of screentime with Michael
Douglas and Shia LaBeouf, Ferlito returned

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:06.700
to theaters in 2010 with a brief supporting
role in Oliver Stone's Wall Street: Money

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:07.930
Never Sleeps.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:12.870
In Stone's Wall Street sequel, inspired by
the 2008 financial crisis, Ferlito plays a

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:15.940
character named Audrey — a tough, no-nonsense
type.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:20.020
It's a role that the Brooklyn native was uniquely
well-suited for.

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:21.269
Stand Up Guys

00:04:21.269 --> 00:04:26.460
Those who saw 2012's Stand Up Guys, starring
Al Pacino and Christopher Walken, likely remember

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:30.880
Ferlito as Sylvia, the woman the protagonists
find in the trunk of their stolen car.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:35.500
The film's subplot involving Ferlito's character
didn't help Stand Up Guys' critical reception.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:39.840
As the victim of brutal abuse, her role moved
the plot, though not everyone felt her character

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.970
was treated with sufficient respect.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:43.520
TIME magazine put it like this:

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:47.930
"It's nice that the stand-up guys rescue and
avenge her, but her suffering is trivialized

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:50.840
in a grossly insensitive way."

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:52.440
Graceland

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:57.660
Ferlito returned to her television crime drama
roots in 2013, joining the cast of USA Network's

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:02.280
Graceland as FBI agent Catherine "Charlie"
DeMarco throughout the series' three-season

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:03.280
run.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:07.120
To prepare for the intense role, Ferlito told
PopSugar that she sat down with a number of

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:10.810
real undercover agents to discuss what the
job is actually like.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:14.410
Though she looked to real-life agents for
inspiration, Ferlito said she didn't study

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:15.410
other actors.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.880
"When I jump into a role, I just kinda go
fresh.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.840
I just jump right in, because you can't focus
on what other people do, or then it's just

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:22.970
not natural."

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:27.150
Graceland benefited greatly from Ferlito's
natural affinity for crime dramas, which is

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:31.720
ultimately the genre in which the actress
truly shines — as NCIS: New Orleans fans

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:32.870
can certainly attest.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:34.010
Thanks for watching!

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:36.550
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:38.650
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

